  "text": "Pthentraken - Boss Guide\n\n​\nGeneral Information\n⬥ Pthentraken has 190,000 LP, across a single fight phase\n⬥ Pthentraken primarily attacks with Magic , with some Ranged  attacks\n​\nOther guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel\n​\nGear, Relics and Familiars\nExample Preset \n​\n\nFight Mechanics\n⬥Stay on the east-side of Pthentraken to avoid pulling Orikalka's aggression\n⬥ You should attack with Ranged \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Arrows give a +27% hit chance boost\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Any other style will only deal insignificant damage\n​\nAttack Rotation\n3x  → Converging Lightning →  →  → Storm Column →\n3x  → Converging Lightning →  →  →\nRepeat\n​\nAuto Attacks (Magic example / Ranged example)\nMechanic: Pthentraken uses Magic  and Ranged  auto attacks.\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ If lower Defence  pray against Magic  / \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Pray  once you are comfortable surviving the mechanics\n​\nConverging Lightning (Example)\nMechanic: Pthentraken summons 3-5 lightning beams around the arena. These beams move towards Pthentraken and deal heavy Magic  damage if you stand in them (up to 5000-5500 damage every 2 ticks).\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ Either:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Wear Insulated boots  to reduce damage taken\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Avoid standing in the lightning beams as they move towards Pthentraken\n​\nStorm Column / Overcharged (Example)\nMechanic: An overhead bar appears above the player. When the bar empties, a 3x3 Storm Column appears on the player's tile, dealing rapidly increasing typeless damage, up to 3600 damage every 2 ticks. It also gives the Overcharged buff.\n​\nWhile Overcharged is active, your hits on Pthentraken deal an additional Magic  hit for 5% of the original damage, and Surge  has a 1-tick cooldown.\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ Move away from the Storm Column as soon as it appears, like in the example video\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Moving too early may make the Storm Column appear at your new location\n​\nHelpful videos\n⬥ Example Pthentraken kills\n​\n\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Pthentraken - Boss Guide ​ General Information ⬥ Pthentraken has 190,000 LP, across a single fight phase ⬥ Pthentraken primarily attacks with Magic , with some Ranged attacks ​ Other guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel ​ Gear, Relics and Familiars Example Preset ​ Fight Mechanics ⬥Stay on the east-side of Pthentraken to avoid pulling Orikalka's aggression ⬥ You should attack with Ranged ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Arrows give a +27% hit chance boost ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Any other style will only deal insignificant damage ​ Attack Rotation 3x → Converging Lightning → → → Storm Column → 3x → Converging Lightning → → → Repeat ​ Auto Attacks (Magic example / Ranged example) Mechanic: Pthentraken uses Magic and Ranged auto attacks. ​ Solution: ⬥ If lower Defence pray against Magic / ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Pray once you are comfortable surviving the mechanics ​ Converging Lightning (Example) Mechanic: Pthentraken summons 3-5 lightning beams around the arena. These beams move towards Pthentraken and deal heavy Magic damage if you stand in them (up to 5000-5500 damage every 2 ticks). ​ Solution: ⬥ Either: ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Wear Insulated boots to reduce damage taken ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Avoid standing in the lightning beams as they move towards Pthentraken ​ Storm Column / Overcharged (Example) Mechanic: An overhead bar appears above the player. When the bar empties, a 3x3 Storm Column appears on the player's tile, dealing rapidly increasing typeless damage, up to 3600 damage every 2 ticks. It also gives the Overcharged buff. ​ While Overcharged is active, your hits on Pthentraken deal an additional Magic hit for 5% of the original damage, and Surge has a 1-tick cooldown. ​ Solution: ⬥ Move away from the Storm Column as soon as it appears, like in the example video ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Moving too early may make the Storm Column appear at your new location ​ Helpful videos ⬥ Example Pthentraken kills ​",
